cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Alea"
abstract: >-
  Alea is a quantum Monte Carlo code for condensed matter calculations in
  two- or three-dimensional materials. It contains variational Monte Carlo,
  diffusion Monte Carlo and path-integral Monte Carlo drivers. It targets
  excitonic complexes in transition-metal dichalcogenides, indirect excitons
  in bilayers, electrons in moiré superlattices and the two-dimensional
  electron gas.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ItaloAlb/alea"
authors:
  - given-names: "Italo Carneiro"
    family-names: "Albuquerque"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3550-1787"
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal do Ceará (UFC)"
keywords:
  - "quantum Monte Carlo"
  - "diffusion Monte Carlo"
  - "path-integral Monte Carlo"
  - "excitons"
  - "two-dimensional materials"
  - "electron gas"
